3.  **`@`**: Matches the literal "at" symbol.
4.  **`[^\s@]+`**: Matches one or more characters that are *not* whitespace and *not* the `@` symbol. This covers the **domain name**.
5.  **`\.`**: Matches a literal dot (`.`). The backslash is necessary because `.` normally means "any character" in regex.
6.  **`[^\s@]+`**: Matches one or more characters that are *not* whitespace and *not* the `@` symbol. This covers the **Top-Level Domain (TLD)**.
7.  **`$`**: Asserts the end of the string.

