/// Counts the number of words in a given string slice.
///
/// A word is defined as any sequence of non-whitespace characters separated by whitespace.
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `text` - A string slice (`&str`) to analyze.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// The total number of words as a `usize`.
fn count_words(text: &str) -> usize {
    // The `split_whitespace()` method splits the string by any amount of whitespace
    // and returns an iterator over the resulting substrings (words).
